  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right now when we create an avatar, we have alot of inconsistency on where the floor is to the avatars foot. sure you can adjust bones to calculate for this, but that is not always the solution to some problems.\nWhat i want is a system in the SDK's avatar descriptor that allows me to set a line where my feet or shoes start that tells VRChat \"My feet start here, this is where i should stand!\"\nMy struggle example i have rn is a pair of sandals i made, where it raises my feet by a couple inches on one outfit. but all my others my feet are relatively the same height vs where the floor should be, this causes my sandals to be sunk completely into the ground.\nI don't think i should have to change my toe bone position in order to fix this issue when i still need that same bone where it is in order for the foot to deform properly when i tippy toe causing the sandal to stay flat as it should.",
